.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt MANET-USER-SCRIPTS.SH 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm manet-user-scripts.sh
.Nd run or inspect staged operator setup scripts
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -list
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs staged scripts in C-locale filename order after provisioning.
Run as root to execute scripts.
Each script runs through its shebang interpreter with working directory
.Pa /
and standard input from
.Pa /dev/null .
The default timeout is 300 seconds per script.
.Pp
Completed scripts, including failures, are skipped on subsequent runs.
A script interrupted before its result was recorded runs again.
Dotfiles, backup suffixes
.Li .disabled , .bak , .orig , ~ ,
subdirectories and files without a shebang are skipped.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -force
Clear recorded results and run all eligible scripts again.
.It Fl -list
List staged filenames and their recorded exit status without running them.
Takes precedence over
.Fl -force .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print help and exit.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/manet-user-scripts/
Staged scripts, normally embedded during flashing.
.It Pa /var/lib/manet-user-scripts.state
Completed script names, exit codes and completion times, separated by tabs.
.It Pa /var/lib/manet-user-scripts.done
Marker that suppresses later automatic service runs.
.It Pa /var/log/manet-user-scripts.log
Appended runner and script output.
.It Pa /etc/mesh.conf
The positive integer
.Li user_script_timeout
overrides the per-script timeout in seconds.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 after listing or running scripts, even when an individual script
fails or times out.
Failures are advisory and do not change the provisioning verdict.
Inspect recorded results or the log.
Unknown arguments return 1.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Repeat the whole script set:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo manet-user-scripts.sh --force
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr manet-provision-status.sh 8 ,
.Xr radio-setup.sh 8
